questionText:
Consider the following reactions (unbalanced).

$$Zn + Hot\,conc.\,{H_2}S{O_4}\mathrel{\mathop{\kern0pt\longrightarrow}
\limits_{}} G + R + XZn + conc.\,NaOH\mathrel{\mathop{\kern0pt\longrightarrow}
\limits_{}} T + QG + {H_2}S + N{H_4}OH\mathrel{\mathop{\kern0pt\longrightarrow}
\limits_{}} Z\,(a\,precipitate) + X + Y$$

Choose the correct option(s).

solution:
(A) $$N{H_4}N{O_3}\mathrel{\mathop{\kern0pt\longrightarrow}
\limits_{below\,300^\circ C}} {N_2}O + 2{H_2}O{N_2}O\mathrel{\mathop{\kern0pt\longrightarrow}
\limits_{above\,600^\circ C}} {N_2} + {O_2}$$
(B) $${(N{H_4})_2}C{r_2}{O_7}\buildrel \Delta \over
\longrightarrow {N_2} + C{r_2}{O_3} + 4{H_2}O$$
(C) $$Ba{({N_3})_2}\mathrel{\mathop{\kern0pt\longrightarrow}
\limits_{180^\circ C}^\Delta } Ba + 3{N_2}$$
(D) $$M{g_3}{N_2}\mathrel{\mathop{\kern0pt\longrightarrow}
\limits_{above\,700^\circ C}} 3Mg + {N_2}$$
Hence, only $${(N{H_4})_2}C{r_2}{O_7}$$ and $$Ba{({N_3})_2}$$ can provide N$_{2}$ gas on heating below $$300^\circ C$$

